sub1:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-bressloff-audit-bressloff-v1-form-constants-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants — Code-to-model traceability: 60/100" ;
        rdfs:comment "Core functions carry docstrings naming the paper location (Eq. 3.12 local harmonics, Eq. 4.9 lateral harmonics, Section 4 / Figs. 16-17 dispersion, Eq. 5.14-5.15 gamma_2 / gamma_3, Section 2 / Eq. 2.1 pullback), presets are named by figure, and the figure panels are labelled with the figures they emulate. -12: branch_selection_for and _make_branch_candidate introduce a scoring functional (mode_count * (lambda A^2/2 + |eta| A^3/3 - denom A^4/4)) and a lattice-local fallback that have no cited equation. -8: planform_modes hard-codes phase scales 0.35, -0.25, 0.5 and -pi/2 offsets with no reference. -8: the clips to +-1.5 on eigenfunction coefficients, safe_denominator, wave_count = 12, sharpness = 2.1 and the tanh rendering nonlinearity are untraced numerical choices. -6: the contoured max-over-phi rendering (lines 729-742) is not tied to the papers' double-map construction, and the calibration-report-to-preset mapping (fig37 -> fig17_even, etc.) is asserted without explanation. -6: the docstring's \"Eq. 3.12 / 4.9\" numbers could not be verified against the 2001 paper's numbering. Evidence: 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L309–L315: local harmonic docstring cites 2001 Eq. 3.12; lateral at 343-345 cites Eq. 4.9 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/68c4a1a/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L309-L315>; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L474–L512: _make_branch_candidate score functional has no equation reference <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/68c4a1a/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L474-L512>; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L660–L691: planform_modes phase scales 0.35, -0.25, 0.5 untraced <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/68c4a1a/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L660-L691>; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L405–L421: np.clip(..., -1.5, 1.5) on perturbative coefficients not in the source <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/68c4a1a/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L405-L421>." ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-code-traceability> ;
        pk:hasProbability "0.6"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-code-traceability> rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants (2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py, docs/media/bressloff_v1_form_constants.gif, bressloff_v1_metrics.csv) satisfies the MorphoEval 0.1.0 criterion 'Code-to-model traceability' for Homo sapiens primary visual cortex (V1) — geometric visual hallucinations (Klüver form constants) and flicker phosphenes" ;
        dcterms:identifier "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Claude Fable 5.1 (primary) + Gemini 4 Argon (independent blinded second assessor)" .
}

